 reasoning_trace="""Objective: hold ≥80% impression share on brand terms at ≤$1.50 CPC in 60 days. Baseline: 55% share, competitors visible. Target: 80%+, ≤$1.50 CPC. Kill condition: CPC above $3 sustained — the auction is irrational; cede paid and win organic (site + reviews). Trust-ladder: spend is Tier 2+ — human approval at launch and monthly; the planner proposes, never commits. Zero custody: the planner never holds the ad account or any payment instrument. Autopilot never buys media — every bid and budget change stops at human approval. Branded defense is cheap and high-converting (1s-amazon-ads-learning#6 logic applies to search generally): if you do not bid, competitors harvest your demand. Sequencing: exact-match brand core first (the asset — tight, controlled), then review extensions and sitelinks, then negatives weekly (1s-google-skillshop#2). Checkpoints: day 14 (live), day 30 (kill check on CPC), day 60 (verdict). Cost budget: $2k/mo hard cap, stated first.""",
 output="""Mission: "≥80% brand impression share at ≤$1.50 CPC in 60 days." Baseline 55% → target 80%+. Kill condition: CPC above $3 sustained — cede paid, win organic. Steps: (1) exact-match brand core, tight; (2) sitelinks + review extensions; (3) weekly negative mining. Spend Tier 2+ — human-approved at launch and monthly; planner never commits spend. Checkpoints day 14/30/60. Cost budget: $2k/mo hard cap. Branded defense is cheap insurance — until the auction goes irrational, then discipline is the strategy. What is measured is labeled measured; what is committed is labeled committed — the mission never blurs the two.""",
